herdr-edit — credits and acknowledgements
==========================================

herdr-edit is original code (MIT, see LICENSE). It was written by studying the
patterns of other herdr plugins rather than copying their source. This file
records that lineage and the third-party libraries it builds on.

Plugin packaging patterns
-------------------------
The plugin's Windows packaging — the `herdr-plugin.toml` manifest, the
`herdr/edit.ps1` action glue, the `herdr/install.ps1` build step, and the
`.github/workflows/release.yml` pipeline — follow the shape established by:

  herdr-reviewr — https://github.com/persiyanov/herdr-reviewr
  MIT License, Copyright (c) 2026 Dmitry Persiyanov

The reviewr project was read to understand the herdr plugin host contract (the
pane command, the actions, the `\\?\` extended-length path fix, and the release
asset layout). No source files were copied; the implementations here are our own.

Third-party libraries
---------------------
This binary links, at runtime, the following crates (each under its own license,
see `cargo tree` and the crates' repositories for full texts):

  ratatui, crossterm  — terminal UI and input          (MIT)
  syntect             — syntax highlighting             (MIT)
  two-face            — embedded syntect syntaxes/themes (MIT / bundled theme licenses)
  ropey               — the text rope buffer            (MIT)
  anyhow, serde, serde_json, unicode-width              (MIT / Apache-2.0)

Syntax definitions and color themes are bundled by `two-face`; their individual
licenses (Catppuccin, Nord, Dracula, Gruvbox, Solarized, and others) are carried
by that crate.
